{
	"name": "Pod Person Aspect",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/commodities/biological/pustules-brown.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 6th level, the spores in your blood whisper a stabilizing mantra to you. You gain resistance to psychic damage.</p><p>In addition, you innately know how to pass as a friend among your enemies. You can attempt to move through the squares of hostile creatures. If they would normally allow an ally to pass, the occupant of the square must make an Insight check against your maneuver DC. If they fail, for a brief instant they mistake you for an ally, they allow you to pass, and this movement doesn’t provoke opportunity attacks from them. If they succeed, you cannot pass but you do not lose any of your movement for your turn. You can use this ability a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier per long rest.</p>",
